IMPORT `g7-art37-43-final`
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`

-- ind-c-tests-art37-43: independent tests (author ind-c) of Part 9, Articles 37 to 43.  Row ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Articles 37 to 43`

GIVEN body IS A `Kind of body that offended under Article 37`
      offence IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `Capacity of a person in relation to a body under Article 37`
      how IS A `How a person comes within a capacity under Article 37`
GIVETH A `Facts for Article 37`
`ind-c Article 37 facts` body offence consent capacity how MEANS
    `Facts for Article 37` WITH
        `kind of body` IS body
        `the body committed an offence under this Law` IS offence
        `consent or connivance is proved` IS consent
        capacity IS capacity
        `how the person comes within the capacity` IS how

GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for Article 37`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c also guilty` facts MEANS `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` facts `the favoured interpretation`

`ind-c the 26(7) penalty` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 3), (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3)

§ `ind-c Article 37 -- offences by corporate and other bodies`

-- A37-01 .. A37-03
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a secretary of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`)
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `ind-c the 26(7) penalty` `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS JUST `ind-c the 26(7) penalty`
-- A37-04: neglect without consent or connivance
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `ind-c the 26(7) penalty` `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A37-05, A37-06: partnerships
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a separate limited partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`)
-- A37-07, A37-08: an unincorporated association, trustees (reading A taken by the encoding at F7.6)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.6`
-- A37-09: a foundation is a body corporate; its council member is its governor
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
-- A37-10, A37-11: a member-managed body corporate; an ordinary member
#ASSERT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT `Art 37(2) the member is treated as a director of the body corporate` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `none of these` `holds the capacity`)
-- A37-12, A37-15: no offence under this Law proved against the body
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a body corporate` FALSE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
-- a partner of an LLP is not a director of it (37(1)(a) pairs each capacity with its body)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-c also guilty` (`ind-c Article 37 facts` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)

§ `ind-c Articles 38 to 43`

-- A39-01, A39-02
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `transitional` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `savings` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `an amendment of this Law` TRUE
-- A39-04: an Order under 2(2) may not amend another provision of the Law consequentially (reading A of F7.14); the other reading by definition
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39 an Order under Article 2(2) may make a consequential amendment of another provision of the Law` `the favoured interpretation`
#ASSERT `Art 39 an Order under Article 2(2) may make a consequential amendment of another provision of the Law` `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.14`
-- A39-06 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): Regulations under 6(3) cannot alter 6(5), 39(2) notwithstanding
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` WITH `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)` IS TRUE, `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)` IS FALSE, `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)` IS FALSE, `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)` IS FALSE, `alters the effect of paragraph (5)` IS TRUE)
-- A41-01 .. A41-04
#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `the Proceeds of Crime (Supervisory Bodies) (Jersey) Law 2008`
#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `an enactment under which the JFSC has functions`
#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `an enactment relating to taxation`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `some other enactment`
-- A43-01
#ASSERT `Art 43 the short title` EQUALS "Charities (Jersey) Law 2014"
